@page
@model Portfolio.Pages.Fun.IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Fun Projects";
}

<header class="page-header"><p class="page-kicker"><i class="bi bi-controller" aria-hidden="true"></i> Personal projects &amp; community</p><h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
@if (ViewData["Message"] is string pageMessage && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(pageMessage))
{
<p class="page-intro">@pageMessage</p>
}
</header>
<section class="content-panel" aria-labelledby="personal-context"><h2 id="personal-context">Personal projects and community</h2><p>These pages preserve the learning, gaming, radio, literary, and technical interests behind my personal projects. My Extra Class amateur radio license is current.</p><p><a asp-page="/AboutMe">About me</a> · <a asp-page="/Tribute">Tribute</a> · <a asp-page="/Skills/TechnicalHistory" asp-fragment="achievements">Personal achievements and earlier technical experience</a> · <a asp-page="/Explore">Full portfolio directory</a></p></section>

<div class="project-grid">
    <article class="project-card">
        <h2>Solarian League Site</h2>
        <p>This fun project was created to help me gain further understanding in the development of front-end
            web applications using C# Blazor WebAsm and SPA. Data is sourced from Discord and an API pass through
            Azure Function App that loads data from Blizzard.</p>
        <p>
            <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" asp-area="" asp-page="/Fun/SolarianLeague">Learn more >></a>
        </p>
    </article>
    <article class="project-card">
        <h2>Ham Radio Go-Kit</h2>
        <p>This is a how to guide to build a Ham Radio Go-Kit for VHF and UHF mobile radio.</p>
        <p>
            <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" asp-area="" asp-page="/Fun/HamRadioVHFGoKit">Learn more >></a>
        </p>
    </article>
</div>
